---
description: Absolute restrictions — never merge PRs, never run migrations. Applies to ALL repos.
alwaysApply: true
---

# NEVER Merge Pull Requests

This is an absolute rule with zero exceptions:

- NEVER run `gh pr merge` or any command that merges a PR
- NEVER approve PRs via CLI or API (`gh pr review --approve`, etc.)
- Your job ends at creating the PR and providing the link
- The human reviews, approves, and merges manually

This applies to ALL repos in all workspaces.

# NEVER Execute Migration Commands

This is an absolute rule with zero exceptions:

- NEVER run `migration:generate`, `migration:generate:local`, or any variant
- NEVER run `migration:run`, `migration:run:local`, or any variant
- NEVER run `migration:revert`, `migration:revert:local`, or any variant
- NEVER run any TypeORM, Prisma, Knex, or other ORM migration CLI command

Your job ends at:
1. Design/modify entities or schema files
2. Provide the exact command for the human to run
3. Wait for the human to confirm the result

This applies regardless of whether the target is local or production. Only the human runs migration commands, always.
